# The trial of pod-relay in podvm (T-326, for PodUtils/podvm@T-1678; calls
# C130 to C134), at podvm main c5b61b45 (commit). The relay legs of
# podvm-ssh go over the blocking facade of pod-relay with the features
# blocking and plain-ws: src/mux.rs is the glue (podvm's Context: the TLS
# roots of pod-tls with the first host bundle, the proxy of the environment,
# no files; the flags and their checks; a node of the given name and node
# token, Pair::for_node; the SSH server of each session on a socketpair; the
# lines of the node by NodeOptions::say, and --once over them; the counts of
# the node; the operator with its --ready-wait and the 10 s goodbye, with no
# end-to-end channel on either leg). src/ws.rs, its handshake and tests,
# src/tls.rs and mux/operator.rs go; the fake relay of the tests keeps its
# own WebSocket server over the frame codec of pod-ws, and refuses a wrong
# token (403) and a second node (409) at the upgrade, as the relay does. The
# wire stays reverse-v1: the hello of version 1, pod-relay's dialect 1.
# Each podcrates tag moves to v0.32.0.
# podvm's tests of its relay (the unit tests of the glue and of the two
# binaries, the fake relay with the real node and operator binaries), the
# SSH test of three authenticated sessions through sshd where the host has
# sshd, podvm's tests of its remote group, clippy of the workspace and
# rustfmt of podvm-ssh as gate.yml runs them, the features of pod-relay in
# the tree, no copy of the moved items left, the runtime-state rows, podvm's
# record gate, each Rust toolchain of the workflows against the
# rust-version of podcrates, and the static check of the node and operator
# binaries for x86_64 musl (podvm's .cargo/config.toml builds them with zig
# cc; a debug build is enough).
cargo test -q -p podvm-ssh --lib --bins --test mux_two_client -- --skip three_authenticated_ssh_sessions
if command -v sshd > /dev/null || [ -x /usr/sbin/sshd ]; then PATH="/usr/sbin:$PATH" cargo test -q -p podvm-ssh --test mux_two_client three_authenticated_ssh_sessions; else echo "adoption: no sshd on this host: the SSH test of the relay did not run"; fi
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm remote::
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-ssh -p podvm --check
cargo tree -q -p podvm-ssh -e features -i pod-relay | grep -q 'pod-relay feature "blocking"'
cargo tree -q -p podvm-ssh -e features -i pod-relay | grep -q 'pod-relay feature "plain-ws"'
test ! -e crates/podvm-ssh/src/ws.rs && test ! -e crates/podvm-ssh/src/tls.rs && test ! -e crates/podvm-ssh/src/mux/operator.rs
! git grep -n -E "fn parse_control|fn emit_control|enum Control|fn read_hello|fn split_node_frame|fn backoff_secs|fn dial_ws|struct TlsConfig|const HELLO_VERSION" -- crates/podvm-ssh
cargo build -q -p podvm-ssh --bins
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (each pod-* crate
# at 0.32.0, with pod-relay and pod-ws); the trial's path form has no row
# for them. Each other row of the patch must be the generated one (base64
# leaves; sha2 0.10.9 comes with pod-relay).
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/node"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/operator"
